name: bitgarth-cli
title: BitGarth CLI
version: '@VERSION@'
summary: Command-line client for BitGarth, a private crypto portfolio tracker
description: |
  BitGarth tracks your Bitcoin and Ethereum holdings without handing your
  financial data to a cloud service. It is watch-only and never asks for
  seed phrases or private keys.

  This snap is the command-line client. It does not sync wallets itself;
  it connects to a BitGarth server you already use, for example:
   - the bitgarth-web snap on this computer (sudo snap install bitgarth-web)
   - your own self-hosted BitGarth (Docker, Homebrew or a release download)
   - the hosted service at https://my.bitgarth.app

  Link the client to your account once, then read your balances:

    bitgarth-cli pair https://my.bitgarth.app/
    bitgarth-cli balancesheet

  For the local bitgarth-web snap, pair with http://127.0.0.1:8080/ and
  add --allow-insecure-http. "login" works as another name for "pair".
  Revoke access any time in the web app under Settings > Paired Clients.

  Website and documentation: https://bitgarth.app

  BitGarth is distributed under the FSL-1.1-ALv2 license.
license: Proprietary
website: https://bitgarth.app
source-code: https://github.com/BitGarth/bitgarth
base: core24
grade: stable
confinement: strict
platforms:
  amd64:
    build-on: [amd64]
    build-for: [amd64]
apps:
  bitgarth-cli:
    command: bin/launch-cli
    plugs: [network]
parts:
  application:
    plugin: dump
    source: payload/
    stage-packages: [ca-certificates]
  launcher:
    plugin: dump
    source: launcher/
    organize:
      launch-cli: bin/launch-cli
